About Neha
Women's Hormone & Weight Loss Coach
My Story
My journey into women's health began long before I became a coach.
Around six years ago, I found myself navigating a series of health challenges that many women silently struggle with. I was diagnosed with endometriosis, underwent surgery, managed hypothyroidism, and faced difficulties conceiving. Like many women, I felt overwhelmed by conflicting health advice and frustrated by the lack of practical solutions that fit into everyday life.
After welcoming my son, I experienced another challenge that many mothers can relate to—weight gain, low energy, and the struggle to prioritise my own health while caring for my family and managing work responsibilities.
Determined to regain my health, I turned to nutrition and lifestyle changes. While many of the meal plans I came across promised results, they often required hours of preparation, complicated recipes, and unrealistic expectations.
As a busy mother with limited support and increasing work commitments, I knew this approach wasn't sustainable.
I began asking myself a simple question:
Why should healthy eating feel so complicated?
Surely women could nourish their bodies, balance their hormones, and achieve their health goals without spending countless hours in the kitchen or following restrictive diets.
That question sparked a passion that would ultimately change the direction of my life.
I immersed myself in learning about nutrition, metabolism, hormonal health, gut health, and sustainable lifestyle practices. What started as a personal mission soon became a professional calling.
To deepen my knowledge and provide evidence-based support to other women, I became a Certified Women's Health Coach and later completed specialist training as a Menopause and Hormone Balancing Coach.
Today, I combine my professional education with my own lived experience to help women navigate the challenges of hormone imbalance, weight gain, digestive issues, low energy, stress, and changing health needs through every stage of life.
Why I Help Women
Women experience unique health challenges that require a unique approach.
From the reproductive years to postnatal recovery, perimenopause, and menopause, our hormones influence everything from metabolism and weight management to mood, energy, sleep, digestion, and overall wellbeing.
Having experienced many of these challenges myself, I understand how frustrating and isolating they can feel.
My mission is to help women stop feeling confused, exhausted, and stuck, and instead feel empowered, educated, and confident in their ability to take control of their health.
I work exclusively with women because I deeply understand their journey and believe they deserve personalised support that recognises the complexities of female health.
My Coaching Philosophy
I believe that sustainable health is built through education, empowerment, and consistency—not perfection.
There is no one-size-fits-all solution when it comes to women's health.
Every woman has a unique lifestyle, health history, hormonal profile, responsibilities, and goals. That's why my coaching approach is highly personalised and designed to fit into real life.
I don't believe in restrictive diets, extreme workouts, or short-term fixes.
Instead, I focus on helping women create lasting lifestyle habits that support:
• Hormonal balance
• Sustainable weight loss
• Metabolic health
• Gut health and digestion
• Emotional wellbeing
• Stress resilience
• Better sleep
• Increased energy
• Long-term health and vitality
My goal isn't just to help women achieve results today—it's to give them the knowledge and tools they need to maintain those results for life.
What Makes My Approach Different
Many health programs focus solely on calories, meal plans, or exercise.
My approach goes deeper.
I take a holistic view of health by looking at the interconnected factors that influence how women feel and function every day.
Rather than simply providing a diet plan to follow, I educate my clients so they understand their bodies and become confident in making informed health decisions.
Together we work on:
✓ Hormone health
✓ Nutrition and metabolism
✓ Macro and micronutrient education
✓ Gut health and digestion
✓ Sleep optimisation
✓ Stress management
✓ Emotional wellbeing
✓ Movement and strength building
✓ Sustainable lifestyle habits
The Hormone Harmony plan is personalised because no two women are the same.
My clients don't leave with another temporary diet.
They leave with a framework for lifelong health.
Business Values
Education First
I believe informed women make empowered health decisions.
Holistic Wellness
Health extends far beyond food and exercise. True wellbeing includes physical, emotional, mental, and hormonal health.
Sustainability
The best health plan is the one you can maintain long-term.
Compassion
Every woman's journey is different, and support should always be free from judgement.
Integrity
I am committed to providing evidence-informed coaching that prioritises long-term health over quick fixes.
Empowerment
My goal is to help women become confident and independent in managing their own health.
Our Vision
To create a world where women understand their bodies, trust their instincts, and have the knowledge and support to thrive through every stage of life.
Our Mission
To empower women over 30 to balance hormones, improve metabolism, achieve sustainable weight loss, and build lifelong health through personalised coaching, education, and holistic lifestyle strategies.

